  "limitations": [
    "SCHED-01 implements initial configuration and exact create replay. SCHED-02 through SCHED-06 retain lease and claim concurrency, occurrence identity, runtime misfire behavior, transactional next-time advancement, and expired-lease recovery.",
    "The configuration service calculates the persisted next UTC value, but the low-level repository trusts an internally constructed validated Schedule. This evidence does not claim cryptographic proof that every internal caller used the recurrence adapter.",
    "The stored digest is an unkeyed consistency seal that detects unrecomputed drift. It does not protect against an administrator who can rewrite both schedule fields and their digest.",
    "SQLite runtime restart behavior and SQLite/PostgreSQL DDL compilation are tested. PostgreSQL runtime transactions and Alembic rollout remain DEL-04 scope.",
    "Timezone-database updates can change later recurrence projections. An already persisted UTC instant remains unchanged until a later scheduler requirement advances it.",
    "Public schedule APIs, authorization, audit and metrics, preview, and the scheduler worker loop remain later API, observability, and scheduler requirements."
  ]
